    "notes": "Blue start course (upper deck of the Verrazzano-Narrows Bridge); the Pink start runs on the lower deck and through Dyker Heights. Route traced over OpenStreetMap streets in the order the race uses them, including the 2026 Bronx change (E 141st St and Third Ave); distances calibrated to features whose distances are published on the course's 2022 USATF certification (NY22001JHP), which predates the Bronx change, so miles 20–21 absorb about 60 m. Elevations from USGS 3DEP 1 m lidar (2014); bare-earth data removes bridges, so the five bridge decks use control points measured from the 2017 NYC lidar (and USGS 2014 lidar for the Verrazzano main span). Downhills are flat on a treadmill without decline. Unofficial.",
